2026-10-13  sfs-plan.sh on the real tree gave the same plan as the
            uploaded copy: 1047 units, 0 hard back edges, 6 cycles.

Stage 0 (host)
--------------
2026-10-13  ch.5 + ch.6 built cleanly up to gcc pass 2 (binutils, gcc,
            glibc with lib64 layout, libstdc++, all temp tools).
            gcc pass 2 log looked stuck for hours: it was not, "tail -f"
            just never exits.  Check stamps / ps instead.

2026-10-13  FAIL  ld inside the chroot: "libz.so.1: cannot open shared
            object file".
            cause  binutils pass 2 linked ld/libbfd/libctf against the
                   HOST zlib (libtool leak; LFS avoids it with a sed on
                   ltmain.sh that the kit had skipped).
            fix    new step 06-zlib: cross build zlib into $SFS before
                   binutils pass 2.  New step 06-check-libs: every ELF in
                   $SFS must find its NEEDED libraries inside $SFS.
            note   first version of check-libs gave false alarms on glibc
                   gconv modules (libJIS.so etc. live next to them,
                   RUNPATH $ORIGIN): same-directory libraries now count.

2026-10-13  NUMJOBS: stage 0 scripts expected "20", sfs-build.sh and the
            SlackBuilds "-j20".  All scripts now accept both.

2026-10-13  README said a new partition is needed: not true.  Any Linux
            fs dir / loop image / btrfs subvolume without noexec.

