      are picked up from the tree by themselves (SCOPE decides); run-time,
      tool, .pc and python edges come automatically; build-only needs
      (headers, find_program, modules) show up as failures -> manual.tsv;
      silent feature losses -> sfs-verify; an override whose sed no longer
      matches stops the build ("override ... changed nothing"); manual.tsv
      lines for removed packages are reported by sfs-plan; seeds that are
      version-bound (gcc-gnat/gdc, rust stage0, go, known_good commits) are
      re-fetched by sfs-seeds.sh; a new download fails loudly offline ->
      new seed.  Possible later feature: an incremental mode that rebuilds
      only changed packages and what depends on them (sfs-deps data).
